# .gitattributes — git-config boilerplate (issue #624, EPIC #616).
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#   Measured 2026-09-14 (issue #608 gap analysis, docs/GIT-TEMPLATES-GAP-ANALYSIS.md):
#   no `.gitattributes` existed, so line-ending normalization and
#   generated/state-path marking were per-editor convention, not enforced.
#   `scripts/check-git-config.sh` (issue #624) checks this file exists and is
#   sane; it does not re-derive these rules, so this file is the declaration.

# --- normalization ----------------------------------------------------------
# Let git decide text vs binary per-file and normalize line endings to LF in
# the repository, converting to the platform's native line ending on checkout.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts and Python must always be LF (a CRLF shebang line breaks exec).
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

# --- explicit binary types this repo has -----------------------------------
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary

# --- generated / runtime-state paths ----------------------------------------
# Mirrors the runtime-state declaration in scripts/check-gitignore.sh
# (issue #625): these paths are generated/runtime output, not authored
# source, so a diff viewer (and GitHub's linguist) should not treat them as
# reviewable prose.
.verify/** linguist-generated=true
*.pyc linguist-generated=true linguist-vendored=true
